\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D40E TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">M</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">O</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Justify your answer.</li>\n<li>State both halves of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-lyapunov\">@thm-lyapunov</span>, and say which of the two\nis the one that certifies stability.</li>\n<li>The induction in the proof of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-lyapunov\">@thm-lyapunov</span> (a) conjugates by a\nunitary matrix whose <strong>last</strong> column is an eigenvector of\n<span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf{A}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D400 TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">A</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. What would go wrong if it were\nthe first column?</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch13-psd-and-svd/06-block-positive-matrices.html"}